b-id-type="pmid">18631387</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b6-ehp-117-a341"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sladek</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Somponpun</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Estrogen receptors: their roles in regulation of vasopressin release for maintenance of fluid and electrolyte homeostasis</article-title><source>Front Neuroendocrinol</source><volume>29</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>114</fpage><lpage>127</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18022678</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-ehp-117-a341"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Use of comparative proteomics to identify potential resistance mechanisms in cancer treatment</article-title><source>Cancer Treat Rev</source><volume>33 </volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>741</fpage><lpage>756</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17854999</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list><notes><title>Editor&#x02019;s note</title><p>In accordance with journal policy, LaPensee et al. were asked whether they wanted to respond to this letter, but they chose not to do so.</p></notes></back></article>